blandaid is descended from https://github.com/Yu-369/VibeCurb. The original
design skills, the pipeline structure, the architecture catalogs, and the CLI
concept are the work of Yu-369 and remain under the MIT license in LICENSE.

Changes from upstream:

  - Every skill was restructured into a router plus on-demand reference files.
  - A shared core skill (blandaid-core) was added so the five generators stop
    redefining the same vocabulary.
  - design-humanizer was added, an auditor for AI design tells, including a
    dated second-order section.
  - Provenance, register selection, and authorship rules were added to core.
  - The CLI was rewritten with real subcommands and five install targets.
  - A validator and CI were added to enforce the project's own writing rules.
  - The project was renamed from VibeCurb to blandaid.

The design-humanizer skill adapts its method from
https://github.com/blader/humanizer by blader, which applies the same approach
to prose using Wikipedia's "Signs of AI writing" guide, maintained by
WikiProject AI Cleanup. The structure of that skill (name the tell, show the
default, show the fix, then guard against over-correction) is a direct debt.
humanizer is MIT licensed. No text was copied from it.

The CLI depends on chalk, inquirer, and ora, distributed under their own
licenses.
